# --- Private-tooling tests (E50_S07_T11) ---
# These tests exercise the private tooling blocklisted above (mcp/router/ and
# skills/mirror-public/) and fail in the public mirror with a missing-dependency
# error if they sync without their subject. They must ship alongside their
# (already-blocklisted) subjects — i.e. stay excluded here too.
# tests/router-prefix-guard.bats: imports mcp/router/allow-list-guard.js
tests/router-prefix-guard.bats
# tests/mirror-orphaned-twin-rewrite.bats: sources skills/mirror-public/scripts/mirror.sh via the helper below
tests/mirror-orphaned-twin-rewrite.bats
# tests/helpers/mirror-orphaned-twin-rewrite.sh: sources skills/mirror-public/scripts/mirror.sh directly
tests/helpers/mirror-orphaned-twin-rewrite.sh
# tests/helpers/router-route.mjs: drives the router that router-prefix-guard.bats imports
tests/helpers/router-route.mjs
# tests/dev-done-post-sync-commit.bats: runs skills/j-dev-done/scripts/commit-post-sync.sh,
# which lives under the fully-private skills/j-dev-done/ blocklisted above. Synced to the
# public mirror without its subject by the 2026-09-18 run (81b7f8b6), where all 14 of its
# cases exit 127 (command not found) and break `npm test` — the exact failure mode the
# "a test may never outlive its subject" rule at the top of this file exists to prevent.
tests/dev-done-post-sync-commit.bats
# tests/mirror-permission-level-invariant.bats: runs skills/j-mirror-public/scripts/mirror.sh,
# which lives under the fully-private skills/j-mirror-public/ blocklisted above (both naming
# forms). Line 48 sets MIRROR_SH to that path and all 12 of its @test cases invoke it, so the
# file has no publicly-meaningful subset — per docs/public-mirror-content-parity.md's rule
# section, option 1 (blocklist) is correct when the ENTIRE file depends on a private subject,
# and a visible skip would skip every case and report nothing. Same failure mode as the
# dev-done-post-sync-commit.bats entry directly above; caught before it reached the mirror.
tests/mirror-permission-level-invariant.bats

# --- Private-tooling playbooks and their tests (E50_S13, user decision 2026-09-10) ---
# brainstorm-to-mirror terminates in `mirror-public`, a deliberately private skill blocklisted
# above in BOTH its bare and j- form. No step-name cutover can make this playbook load in the
# public mirror, because skills/j-mirror-public/SKILL.md is never shipped there — load-playbooks.sh
# requires every step's skills/<dir>/SKILL.md to exist or it skips the whole playbook. Rather than
# publish mirror-public or swap the terminal step for a public skill, the playbook itself is
# private tooling and is blocklisted. The loader's skip behaviour was never the defect.
skills/jenga/playbooks/brainstorm-to-mirror.json
.claude/skills/jenga/playbooks/brainstorm-to-mirror.json
.agents/skills/jenga/playbooks/brainstorm-to-mirror.json
# understand-then-ship was blocklisted here only because it composed brainstorm-to-mirror — it had
# no private step of its own. E53_S10_T01 repointed it at the public idea-to-committed playbook and
# renamed it understand-then-commit, so it now ships publicly and is deliberately NOT listed here.
# The two real-catalog tests assert those now-private playbooks load against the real skills tree,
# so they follow their subjects out of the mirror per the E50_S07_T11 rule directly above. This is
# what turns the public suite's two failures green — because their subjects are private, NOT by
# weakening either assertion; both still run in full in the private repo.
# tests/load-playbooks-stepobject.bats: asserts the real brainstorm-to-mirror.json loads
tests/load-playbooks-stepobject.bats
# tests/load-playbooks-composition.bats: its real-catalog check used to assert the (then-private)
# understand-then-ship composition. Since E53_S10_T01 that check targets two PUBLIC playbooks
# (understand-then-commit -> idea-to-committed), so the private-subject rationale above no longer
# applies to this entry. It is left in place only because E50_S20_T02 owns both of these test
# entries and their visible-skip conversion; unblocking it is that task's call, not this one's.
tests/load-playbooks-composition.bats

